{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b4e62fbf-fc74-4066-9d5e-f01c44f33be7",
    "name": "VidaCruz API",
    "description": "API REST de VidaCruz (triaje y asistente clínico). Los tests (pm.test) comprueban los códigos y los campos esperados.\n\n**Requisitos:** el stack levantado con `run.ps1` / `run.sh` (Docker Compose), Postman de escritorio, el entorno `VidaCruz local` con las dos API keys (están en el `.env` de la plataforma) y, para las consultas clínicas, `GEMINI_API_KEY` en ese `.env`.\n\n**Orden:** ejecutar las carpetas de arriba abajo (Collection Runner). Las peticiones comparten variables (`patientId`, `urgencyBaseline`).\n\n**Fuera de la colección:** la prueba de resiliencia (detener el asistente con `docker compose stop assistant-service` y comprobar que el triaje sigue registrando) es manual.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Salud y autenticación",
      "description": "Los probes son públicos; todo lo demás exige X-API-Key. El 401 no distingue entre clave ausente y clave incorrecta.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 Readiness del triaje (sin clave)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{triageUrl}}/actuator/health/readiness",
              "host": [
                "{{triageUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "health",
                "readiness"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 y UP, sin necesitar API key\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"UP\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 Readiness del asistente (sin clave)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{assistantUrl}}/actuator/health/readiness",
              "host": [
                "{{assistantUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "health",
                "readiness"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 y UP, sin necesitar API key\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"UP\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.3 Triaje sin API key",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{triageUrl}}/triage/pacientes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": [
                "{{triageUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "triage",
                "pacientes",
                "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"401 UNAUTHORIZED\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"UNAUTHORIZED\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.4 Triaje con API key incorrecta",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "wrong-key-0123456789"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{triageUrl}}/triage/pacientes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": [
                "{{triageUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "triage",
                "pacientes",
                "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"401 UNAUTHORIZED y no repite la clave enviada\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"UNAUTHORIZED\");",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include(\"wrong-key\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.5 Asistente sin API key",
          "request": {
